  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-cursor-theme",
      "text": "> 🖱️ Per-state mouse cursor customization for DeepSeek Harness — give every UI state (default, pointer, text, wait, not-allowed, …) its own PNG/CUR cursor, applied live and persisted across restarts."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-cursor-theme",
      "text": "[中文文档](README.zh.md) · [Requirements](docs/requirements.md) · [Feasibility](docs/feasibility.md) · Published on [npm](https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-cursor-theme) · Listed on [DSH 1024Store](https://github.com/imsai-sh/awesome-deepseek-harness-plugins/blob/main/catalog/plugins/auki-zy--dsh-cursor-theme.json) · Listed on [dshfind](https://dshfind.com) · [Release SOP](docs/PUBLISHING.md)\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-cursor-theme",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"data/theme-packs/promo-banner.png\" alt=\"dsh-cursor-theme — 19 themes × 14 states\" width=\"100%\" />\n</p>\n\n> Every cell above shows all **14 mouse states** of one theme. The last cell (dashed border + **Personal** badge) is a personal theme — fork the repo, add your own pack, and it joins the lineup with its own style.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "✨ Features",
      "text": "- 🎯 **Per-UI-state overrides** — 14 mouse states (default, pointer, text, wait, help, not-allowed, grab, grabbing, progress, cell, copy, move, resize-ew, resize-ns), each with its own image, hotspot and size\n- 🎨 **18 original preset themes** — every theme covers **all 14 states** with baked PNGs:\n  - 6 color palettes: Aurora, Honey, Mint, Sunset, Graphite, High Contrast\n  - 12 creative themes: **Paw 🐾 · Energy ⚡ · Neon 🌃 · Emoji 😀 · Pixel 👾 · Weather ⛅ · Origami 📐 · Astro 🧑🚀 · Candy 🍬 · Ghost 👻 · Hi-Vis XL 🔍 (48px) · Pop 🎈**\n  - One click to apply; every theme is also downloadable as a ZIP image pack\n- 🖼️ **Built-in SVG template library** (25 hand-drawn shapes) + upload your own PNG/CUR (≤128×128, ≤5 MB validated)\n- 📦 **Image pack import/export** — one ZIP (a PNG per state + `manifest.json`), inspect/edit/share real image files, or generate with an AI\n- 🪟 **Apply to system (Windows)** — one click writes the theme into the OS cursor scheme (registry + `SPI_SETCURSORS`), visible in Explorer and every app; macOS: experimental Swift overlay + Accessibility guidance\n- 📍 **Hotspot editor** (X/Y) for pixel-accurate clicks · 🔍 size steps 16/24/32/48\n- 👁️ Per-row finished-cursor preview (ri"
    },
    {
      "section": "📦 Install",
      "text": "```sh"
    },
    {
      "section": "DSH Desktop (the GUI runs the `desktop` profile) — also installable from the Community Market (1024Store)",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile desktop add dsh-cursor-theme"
    },
    {
      "section": "Plain dsh web / browser (optional)",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add dsh-cursor-theme\n```\n\nRestart DSH Desktop (or reload `dsh web`), then open **Settings → Cursor Theme**."
    },
    {
      "section": "🎯 Usage",
      "text": "| Action | How |\n|---|---|\n| Apply a preset theme | Settings → Cursor Theme → click a theme pill |\n| Download a theme as ZIP | Click the download icon next to a theme |\n| Customize one state | Edit next to a state row → upload PNG/CUR or pick a built-in shape → set hotspot/size |\n| Import a ZIP pack | Image pack → Import (e.g. a pack generated by an AI) |\n| Apply to the whole OS (Windows) | Apply to system → one click |\n| Reset everything | Restore system default |"
    },
    {
      "section": "🎨 Personal Theme — fork your own",
      "text": "The cell with the **Personal** badge (dashed border, listed last) is *your* theme — the bundled `cat-sitiao` is an example. Two ways to make your theme permanent:\n\n**Option A — ZIP pack (no code)**\n1. In DSH: Settings → Cursor Theme → **Import** any ZIP image pack (PNGs + `manifest.json` — export one of the built-ins as a starting template, or generate one with the included AI prompt)\n2. Keep the ZIP in your own notes / repo to re-import anywhere"
    },
    {
      "section": "🎨 Personal Theme — fork your own",
      "text": "**Option B — Fork the repo (recommended for contributors)**\n1. **Fork** this repository (a fork is your own copy — you manage it independently)\n2. In `scripts/theme-art.mjs` add your theme entry (copy an existing one, change the palette or SVG art), or drop your own pack at `data/themes-personal.json` with `{ \"schema\": 1, \"name\": \"...\", \"states\": { ... } }`\n3. Run `node scripts/generate-theme-packs.mjs && node scripts/generate-assets.mjs` to bake it\n4. Apply it in Settings → Cursor Theme, or publish your fork / open a PR to share it"
    },
    {
      "section": "🎨 Personal Theme — fork your own",
      "text": "> Your fork is yours — customize freely, keep your own palette and icons, and don't worry about upstream changes (your fork is independent)."
    },
    {
      "section": "🛠️ Development",
      "text": "```sh\nnpm install\nnpm run check    # typecheck + build + test\nnpm run build    # host lib/ + client client/client.js\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Asset pipeline",
      "text": "- `scripts/theme-art.mjs` — original hand-drawn art for the 12 creative themes (per-state SVG + decorators: glow / gloss / dots)\n- `scripts/generate-theme-packs.mjs` — renders every theme into 32×32 (or 48×48) PNGs via `@resvg/resvg-js`, emits `data/theme-packs/<id>.zip` (image packs) + `data/themes-<id>.json`\n- `scripts/generate-assets.mjs` — merges packs into `data/assets.json` (built-in preset catalog)\n- Client is bundled by esbuild into a single file (`client/client.js`), with react and `@deepseek-ai/*` kept external (injected by the host `__ModuleLoader__`)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Market catalog",
      "text": "- `docs/catalog/manifest.json` + `docs/catalog/v1/plugins.json` — standard DSH Community Market catalog source (v1 contract), deployable to any host that serves JSON with the right content-type (e.g. Cloudflare Pages / Vercel)\n- npm publishing: `npm publish` (requires a public npm token with *bypass 2FA* for publishing)"
    },
    {
      "section": "📁 Layout",
      "text": "```\n├── package.json            # dsh.bundle + dsh.client declarations\n├── cordis.patch.yml        # layer insertion patch\n├── docs/\n│   ├── feasibility.md      # feasibility analysis"
    },
    {
      "section": "📄 License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
  ],
